WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.360 --> 00:00:01.350
- Or how have you rather,

00:00:01.350 --> 00:00:02.650
been getting your message

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:05.310
to young people since the trip?

00:00:05.310 --> 00:00:06.960
Because that's, you
can have such an impact

00:00:06.960 --> 00:00:07.980
on the younger generation.

00:00:07.980 --> 00:00:09.870
So, how do you do that?

00:00:09.870 --> 00:00:11.370
- It's so wild to even hear you say that

00:00:11.370 --> 00:00:13.350
because if you would've
asked me a few years ago,

00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:15.300
like, if I knew that

00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:17.790
I was gonna be impacting
people the way I am.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.650
I knew I did it with my music and my dance

00:00:19.650 --> 00:00:23.130
but to be doing it for
this is just, it's so,

00:00:23.130 --> 00:00:26.100
I can't even tell you how
I feel about it, but I,

00:00:26.100 --> 00:00:27.810
of course, I'm doing
my social media videos

00:00:27.810 --> 00:00:30.630
of talking about it, but I'm
also going to schools now

00:00:30.630 --> 00:00:31.890
and I'm speaking at the schools,

00:00:31.890 --> 00:00:34.590
which to me is something I'm
so incredibly passionate about.

00:00:34.590 --> 00:00:35.700
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- Because I'm going there,

00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:37.110
I'm in their faces, I'm talking to them.

00:00:37.110 --> 00:00:38.580
Some of them may follow
me or know me already

00:00:38.580 --> 00:00:40.680
but now I'm sitting there
talking about Holocaust education

00:00:40.680 --> 00:00:42.930
and they're relating to
it in a different way.

00:00:42.930 --> 00:00:45.060
I also did a Concert for Kindness

00:00:45.060 --> 00:00:47.250
that was a concert to promote kindness

00:00:47.250 --> 00:00:49.170
and combat anti-Semitism,

00:00:49.170 --> 00:00:51.330
and anything I could do to just continue,

00:00:51.330 --> 00:00:53.250
continue to spread no hate,

00:00:53.250 --> 00:00:56.040
no form of hate and anti-Semitism.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:57.690
- I mean, it's so funny
'cause you were like,

00:00:57.690 --> 00:00:59.250
you know, wasn't your original thing,

00:00:59.250 --> 00:01:01.530
but it's interesting how life

00:01:01.530 --> 00:01:03.270
will put you on this path
that you have no idea

00:01:03.270 --> 00:01:05.580
you're even taking, you're
just doing you, you know?

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:08.730
And it's incredible how you
have this huge following

00:01:08.730 --> 00:01:09.840
and you're able to educate

00:01:09.840 --> 00:01:12.540
while having a good time at the same time.

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.460
'Cause that's what life should be about,

00:01:14.460 --> 00:01:15.750
learning and then also just

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:16.950
having a good time with everybody.

00:01:16.950 --> 00:01:20.370
- And I wish more people
would use their platforms for-

00:01:20.370 --> 00:01:21.510
- [Kelly] Absolutely.
- Just to stand up

00:01:21.510 --> 00:01:22.947
for whatever they believe in.

00:01:22.947 --> 00:01:24.333
- Absolutely.

00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:28.020
Well, you were recently
honored in Washington DC

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.030
for your dedication to anti-Semitism,

00:01:30.030 --> 00:01:31.800
so, congratulations on that, first of all.

00:01:31.800 --> 00:01:33.330
- Thank you.
- [Kelly] That's incredible.

00:01:33.330 --> 00:01:37.590
But what was that like, that visit?

00:01:37.590 --> 00:01:38.730
- Ugh, I still can't even believe

00:01:38.730 --> 00:01:40.440
that I was there, honestly.

00:01:40.440 --> 00:01:41.790
But I was there for the first ever

00:01:41.790 --> 00:01:44.430
Woman's Jewish Forum,
which was incredible.

00:01:44.430 --> 00:01:47.010
And then I also got to
have a one-on-one meeting

00:01:47.010 --> 00:01:49.560
with Doug Emhoff, who is
the first Second Gentleman

00:01:49.560 --> 00:01:52.200
and of course, the Vice
President, Kamala Harris' husband.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.120
- [Kelly] Yeah.
- And he is a Jewish man.

00:01:54.120 --> 00:01:57.330
He recently went to Auschwitz himself

00:01:57.330 --> 00:01:59.970
and had a really intense
experience as well.

00:01:59.970 --> 00:02:01.560
So he found out about my series

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.440
and we sat down and we
talked about our experiences

00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:05.400
and our family's history,

00:02:05.400 --> 00:02:07.260
and also how we're both continuing

00:02:07.260 --> 00:02:11.070
in our separate ways to continue
to combat anti-Semitism.

00:02:11.070 --> 00:02:12.210
- Yeah.

00:02:12.210 --> 00:02:14.073
Can you imagine, I always think,

00:02:14.910 --> 00:02:16.290
like, if your grandparents,

00:02:16.290 --> 00:02:18.000
you know, could see what you're doing now,

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.670
like it's an incredible,
it's an incredible thing,

00:02:20.670 --> 00:02:21.503
that's what I'm saying.

00:02:21.503 --> 00:02:23.850
They survived something
and like now you're able to

00:02:23.850 --> 00:02:25.560
keep that legacy going of,

00:02:25.560 --> 00:02:26.910
you know, bringing people information

00:02:26.910 --> 00:02:29.580
and not losing what happened
so you don't forget,

00:02:29.580 --> 00:02:30.660
so we don't repeat history.

00:02:30.660 --> 00:02:33.150
It's really cool, like
that full circle moment.

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:36.240
And I can't imagine watching
your daughter, you know?

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:38.730
And carrying this legacy
on with your family.

00:02:38.730 --> 00:02:41.070
So, what is the most important thing

00:02:41.070 --> 00:02:43.023
you want our audience to hear today?

00:02:44.340 --> 00:02:47.520
- It's also, it's really amazing

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:50.760
and I know my Zadie, my
grandfather is watching down

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.860
and I know he's here right now
with all of us watching this,

00:02:52.860 --> 00:02:54.480
so this is really powerful for me

00:02:54.480 --> 00:02:56.130
to be able to be here and do this.

00:02:56.130 --> 00:02:58.530
But, you know, speaking of my grandfather,

00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:00.360
back then then before
the Holocaust, you know?

00:03:00.360 --> 00:03:02.220
He was very popular
amongst all his friends,

00:03:02.220 --> 00:03:03.810
of all his non-Jewish friends.

00:03:03.810 --> 00:03:06.480
And the second the
announcements happened with,

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:07.320
you know, everything about

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:10.350
how terrible the Jewish people
are and about the Holocaust,

00:03:10.350 --> 00:03:12.510
all his friends that he was
friends with his entire life

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:14.370
completely turned on him, beat him up,

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:16.860
spit on him, said, "You
dirty Jew, get away."

00:03:16.860 --> 00:03:19.650
Friends that he was friends
with his entire life, right?

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:21.810
- Wow.
- So, imagine that?

00:03:21.810 --> 00:03:23.850
Imagine people nowadays that happening,

00:03:23.850 --> 00:03:26.040
and it does happen and it is happening.

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.457
So that's why when people say,

00:03:27.457 --> 00:03:29.430
"The Holocaust can never happen", it can.

00:03:29.430 --> 00:03:31.650
I mean, in Los Angeles
being here all the time,

00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:33.870
two Jewish men were shot
outside of their temple

00:03:33.870 --> 00:03:36.060
just for being Jewish, recently.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:40.800
And there, Jewish crime,
anti-Semitism, it's so huge now.

00:03:40.800 --> 00:03:43.860
It's one of the biggest
crime, like, hate crimes now.

00:03:43.860 --> 00:03:47.310
So, and it's such a small
percentage of the population.

00:03:47.310 --> 00:03:49.350
So it's like we, this starts with us,

00:03:49.350 --> 00:03:51.150
we all need to come together to make sure

00:03:51.150 --> 00:03:53.040
we end this together.

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:54.185
- Absolutely.

00:03:54.185 --> 00:03:55.438
(audience applauding)

